# Customer registration, in order. After each step request the token again in auth.http:
# the registration_status claim moves forward (REGISTER -> PROFILE -> KYC -> COMPLETE).
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api/v1/user/register
@registerToken = PASTE_TOKEN_FROM_auth.http

### STEP 1 - Register (public): creates the user in Keycloak and in user_db
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ana.martinez92@gmail.com",
  "password": "secure1!",
  "phoneCode": "+52",
  "phoneNumber": "6649876543"
}

### STEP 2 - Request the token in auth.http and verify the email with the link sent to
### Mailpit (http://localhost:8025). Required before the KYC step.

### Resend the verification email
POST {{baseUrl}}/me/verify-email
Authorization: Bearer {{registerToken}}

### Fix a mistyped email (before KYC); a new verification is sent and you log in with the new email
PUT {{baseUrl}}/me/email
Authorization: Bearer {{registerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ana.martinez92@gmail.com"
}

### STEP 3 - Profile (birthday as dd/MM/yyyy)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/me/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{registerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "names": "Ana",
  "firstSurname": "Martinez",
  "secondSurname": "Lopez",
  "gender": "FEMALE",
  "birthday": "15/06/1992",
  "countryOfBirth": "MX"
}

### STEP 4 - KYC: CURP and RFC must match each other and the name and birthday.
### Assigns CUSTOMER_BASIC and requests the account from account-service (Kafka)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/me/kyc
Authorization: Bearer {{registerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "curp": "MALA920615MSLRPN09",
  "rfc": "MALA920615AB3",
  "documentType": "NATIONAL_ID_CARD"
}

### STEP 5 (optional) - Financial information
PUT {{baseUrl}}/me/financial
Authorization: Bearer {{registerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "occupationType": "EMPLOYEE",
  "employerName": "Tech Company SA de CV",
  "incomeSource": "SALARY",
  "monthlyIncome": 25000.00,
  "maritalStatus": "SINGLE"
}
